{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>וַיִּשְׁכֹּן יִשְׂרָאֵל בֶּטַח</b> — when? When they will be בָּדָד (alone), and the statement ״וַיִּשְׁכֹּן״ continues with the statement above it, which is ״וַיֹּאמֶר הַשְׁמֵד״ — that HaShem commanded Israel to destroy every soul among the inhabitants of the land, and thereby ״וַיִּשְׁכֹּן יִשְׂרָאֵל בֶּטַח בָּדָד״." "And its saying <b>עֵין יַעֲקֹב</b> means to say that even though their eye will be toward a land of grain and wine — meaning, to eat of its fruit and to be sated from its goodness — even so they will not kick when there will no longer be nations dwelling with them in the land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The text reads ״וַיֹּאמֶר הַשְׁמֵד״, evidently a contracted citation of the prior verse (Deut. 33:27) blended with the command to destroy the inhabitants; rendered as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:26.132084529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}